# SEP Boot ROM sanity preload — SystemC test fixture.
#
# One 64-bit word per line in big-endian ASCII hex (MSB first).
# Blank lines and `#`-prefixed comments are ignored, matching the
# upstream hex format produced by the SMC tooling.
#
# The first four words are the SEP fast-boot stub copied verbatim from
# `dv/smc/tb/meta/scripts/bootrom_sanity.rv64.hex` in tt-oca-hw.
# Subsequent rows include a sparse non-zero sentinel to verify that the
# preload pipeline correctly stores words at offset > 0.
#
# Word 0: SEP fast-boot stub — instruction word 1
000005177c105073
# Word 1: fast-boot stub — instruction word 2
3055107301450513
# Word 2: fast-boot stub — instruction word 3
3046b073fff00693
# Word 3: fast-boot stub — instruction word 4
ffdff06f10500073
# Words 4..6: zero padding (also implicit; included to exercise the
# parser's blank-data-word path).
0000000000000000
0000000000000000
0000000000000000
# Word 7: sentinel — verifies sparse non-zero placement.
0000DEADBEEF1234
